---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ClosingCalculator from '../../../components/calculator/ClosingCalculator';

const seo = {
  title: 'Closing Costs in Roatán – Buyer & Seller Guide | The Agency Roatán',
  description: 'What are the real closing costs when buying or selling property in Roatán? Transfer tax, legal fees, commission, VAT, and capital gains — with a live calculator.',
};

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: seo.title,
  description: seo.description,
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'HowTo',
    name: 'How to estimate closing costs in Roatán',
    description: 'Estimate buyer and seller closing costs for a Roatán property transaction.',
    step: [
      { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Enter purchase or selling price' },
      { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Select purchase structure (asset or corporation)' },
      { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Add legal fees, commissions, and prorated items' },
      { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Review the itemized breakdown and total cost to close' },
    ],
  },
};
---

<Base title={seo.title} description={seo.description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Buying Guide</p>
      <h1>Closing Costs in Roatán</h1>
      <p class="hero-intro">
        A clear breakdown of what buyers and sellers actually pay at closing —
        with a live calculator to estimate your transaction costs before you commit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="calc-section">
    <div class="container">
      <ClosingCalculator client:load />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section">
    <div class="container guide-body prose">

      <h2>What buyers pay</h2>
      <p>
        As a buyer in Roatán, your closing costs typically fall into four categories: transfer tax,
        legal fees, any prorated items (HOA, insurance, services), and — if you're setting up a
        Honduran corporation to hold the property — a one-time incorporation cost.
      </p>

      <h3>Transfer Tax (3%)</h3>
      <p>
        When buying a property directly (an "asset purchase"), a 3% transfer tax is levied on the
        registered value. This is paid at the time of registration with the Honduran Property Registry.
        If the seller holds the property inside a Honduran corporation and you buy the shares of that
        corporation rather than the property directly, no transfer tax applies — because ownership of
        the property itself hasn't changed, only the corporate shareholder has.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a common structure for higher-value transactions and is completely legal. Your attorney
        will advise on whether it makes sense for your purchase.
      </p>

      <h3>Legal Fees (typically 2–3%)</h3>
      <p>
        You'll need a licensed Honduran attorney (not just a notary). Your attorney drafts the sales
        contract, conducts title due diligence at the Property Registry, advises on structure, and
        registers the transfer. Fees generally run 2–3% of the purchase price; some attorneys charge a
        flat fee for smaller transactions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Don't skip title due diligence. Honduras uses a public property registry, and most title issues
        are discoverable with a proper search — but only if someone actually does one.
      </p>

      <h3>Prorated Items</h3>
      <p>
        At closing, the buyer reimburses the seller for prepaid expenses covering the period after the
        closing date. Common prorated items include HOA fees (typically billed annually), property
        insurance, and recurring services. The calculator above handles this automatically once you
        enter a closing date.
      </p>

      <hr class="section-rule" />

      <h2>What sellers pay</h2>
      <p>
        Sellers carry the larger share of closing costs. The three main items are the agent commission,
        VAT on the commission, and capital gains tax if the property has appreciated.
      </p>

      <h3>Agent Commission (typically 6%)</h3>
      <p>
        In Roatán, commissions are conventionally paid entirely by the seller. The listing agent and the
        buyer's agent split the commission between them — the buyer does not pay a separate fee. The
        standard rate is 6%, though this can vary by transaction type and agreement.
      </p>

      <h3>VAT on Commission (15%)</h3>
      <p>
        Honduras charges 15% VAT (Impuesto Sobre Ventas) on services, including real estate
        commissions. The VAT is applied to the full commission amount and is a seller expense. On a 6%
        commission, the effective total cost to the seller is 6% × 1.15 = 6.9% of the selling price.
      </p>

      <h3>Capital Gains Tax</h3>
      <p>
        Capital gains are taxed on the net gain — selling price minus commission minus your cost basis
        (land + improvements + acquisition costs). The applicable rate depends on your structure
        (individual vs. corporation), residency status, and holding period. A common planning rate is
        4%, but consult a Honduran tax attorney for your specific situation — especially if you've held
        the property for many years or made significant improvements.
      </p>

      <h3>Municipal Taxes</h3>
      <p>
        Any unpaid municipal property taxes must typically be cleared at or before closing. The amount
        varies by municipality and property value. Your attorney will confirm what's owed.
      </p>

      <hr class="section-rule" />

      <div class="cta-band">
        <p class="cta-heading">Ready to run the numbers on a specific property?</p>
        <p class="cta-sub">I can walk you through closing costs for any listing before you make an offer.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary">Talk to Tomas</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--plaster);
    border-bottom: var(--hairline);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-5xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--iron);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
  }

  .hero-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--iron-60);
    max-width: 60ch;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .calc-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-16);
  }

  .guide-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-24);
    background: var(--plaster);
    border-top: var(--hairline);
  }

  .guide-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-chic);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    color: var(--iron);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .guide-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .guide-body h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--iron);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .guide-body p {
    color: var(--iron-60);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .section-rule {
    border: none;
    border-top: var(--hairline);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  .cta-band {
    background: var(--iron);
    padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  .cta-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--canvas);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .cta-sub {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.60);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--agency-red);
    color: var(--canvas);
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.88;
  }
</style>
